                <pb facs="0265" n="175" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg175"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">722.65/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hartman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-05T17:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">November 5,
                                1919—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 6—8:20
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>My October 2 noon. Bill based on amended memorandum authorizing President to make
                    contract <hi rendition="#italic">ad referendum</hi> for loan of 40,000,000
                    sucres and including other provisions reported in my said telegram of October 2
                    noon, passed by Congress.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
